        "original_id": "c57782ad-139d-5de5-8fd2-305747ee5d39",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Peter Hackett, Captain James Estill\n- Places: Cumberland Gap, Wilderness Road, Virginia, Kentucky, Tennessee, Cumberland Mountains, Appalachian Mountains\n- Topics: Scotch-Irish migration\n\nFacts:\n- In approximately 1771, Peter Hackett was bonded out to Captain James Estill.\n- In the late 18th century, Peter Hackett was part of the broad Scotch-Irish migration along the Wilderness Road through the Cumberland Gap from Virginia into what later became known as Kentucky.\n- The Cumberland Gap is a narrow pass through the long ridge of the Cumberland Mountains within the Appalachian Mountains.\n- The Cumberland Gap is near the junction of the U.S. states of Kentucky, Virginia, and Tennessee.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
